c(6, "§0.1; §0.1 table (verbatim); §3.2", "monetization", "People chose this app because it is free, has no ads and does not paywall habits: U:free_model_any 39 of 86 (45.35%, CI 35.3–55.8%, 4.97★) (verbatim): " + table("## 0.1 People chose this app", 0) + " — reviewers had already met paywalls elsewhere: 'most of them only let you make around 4 habits before tealling you to pay. This one let me make as many as I wanted (10 so far)!'; 'almost all of them need some sort of payment… rivalling paid habit trackers'; 'Why anyone would be pay a monthly sub for an app like habitkit, which offers no benefit over this app, I haven't a clue'; 'I sat down to write a similar app because the alternatives have paid subscriptions. GPT suggested I look at this app; I downloaded it and immediately closed Xcode' (ru); U:paywall_contrast 16 (18.60%), all 5★.", "free, no ads, unlimited habits, no IAP", "purchase-driver", "free_model_any 39 / 45.35% / 4.97★; MODEL_FREE 30; NO_ADS 12; NO_PAYWALL 7; VS_PAID 7; UNLIMITED 3; paywall_contrast 16 / 18.60%", "build-free", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13903380759", "13469159788", "13546859530", "14227392787", "14458611566"], "'free with no habit cap' is itself the positioning against the category", "")

c(7, "§0.2; §3.3; §3.4", "insight", "What they value in the product: simplicity, then the grid — U:simplicity 40 (46.51%, CI 36.3–57.0%; PRAISE_EASE 27, PRAISE_SIMPLE 20): 'Everything you need, and nothing more… no fancy or overly complicated features'; 'Nothing superfluous, aesthetic, beautiful, intuitive' (ru); 'without extra noise'; U:visual_progress 16 (18.60%; PRAISE_VISUAL 10, PRAISE_STATS_VIEWS 9): 'remind me of github, very beautiful'; 'progress by day, week, for the year, clear statistics, beautiful visualisation. You can mark progress for past days and add a note. Ideal'; 'It is very motivating when you see your progress for the year'; widgets the third strength (PRAISE_WIDGETS 8: 'keep a widget on my home screen, and tick the specific habit… and that's it!').", "grid + stats + widgets, minimal", "praise", "simplicity 40 / 46.51%; visual_progress 16 / 18.60%; WIDGETS 8 / 9.30%", "build-free", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13682234945", "13766824285", "13888489114", "13733717410", "13958506607", "14170605260", "13787454014"], "", "")

c(8, "§0.3; §2.3 (future charging); §5.4; §8.4", "product-rule", "The main risk in this corpus is a change to the free model: the developer's terms reserve the right to 'charge for their services at any time'; two reviewers attach their loyalty to the price (U:future_pricing 2, 2.33%): 'I really hope it stays free, otherwise I will have to find a different habit tracker'; 'I hope it won't become a subscription, or at least that there will be an option to buy it once!' (ru) — the only statements in the corpus that make continued use conditional on anything, and the condition is price; the free model is the reason 45.35% give, and three name habit limits or subscriptions as what they avoid elsewhere.", "free now; terms reserve charging", "mixed", "future_pricing 2 / 2.33%; free_model_any 45.35%", "product-rule", "Meaningful (n=2)", "generalisable", ["13682234945", "13936987753", "13903380759", "13546859530", "14227392787"], "", "")

